:name: statemachined on an emulated Uno R4 Minima
:description: The reference board under Renode, for testing firmware/hal/.

# What this is for, and what it is not for:
#
# It exercises the code the host build physically cannot compile -- the pin map,
# the port-register arithmetic, the timer ISR, and a whole session over a real
# UART peripheral. That is otherwise covered by nothing at all.
#
# It says nothing about timing. Renode runs on virtual time against a nominal
# MIPS figure, so a scan here takes however long we tell it to. The 10 kHz claim
# needs a board. See dev/HARDWARE.md.

$elf?=@.pio/build/uno_r4_minima_sci/firmware.elf

using sysbus
mach create "statemachined"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $ORIGIN/statemachined-uno-r4.repl

# The SCI build, not the USB one: the host is on SCI2 (D0/D1). See the note in
# firmware/hal/renesas_ra4m1.cpp.
sysbus LoadELF $elf

# No `showAnalyzer sysbus.sci2` here on purpose: the Robot tests attach their own
# terminal tester to that UART, and the two fight over it -- symptom is a device
# that is demonstrably running and answering while the test sees nothing at all.
# For interactive use, attach one yourself after including this file.
